ower_Switch` net, which feeds `J1.15`/`J1.16` \u2014 the EPD panel's `VDDIO`/`VDD` pins per the PDI pin table\"}], \"impact\": \"The panel's VDD may remain powered when the display power switch is off. This defeats the leakage-prevention function and could cause the panel to leak or misbehave.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The most likely anomaly is that SKW92A pins LAN_PORT3_TX+/- (U2.13/U2.14) are shorted to the GND net, which is not a design intent. A lower-confidence concern is that the EPD FPC VDD pin is on the always-on +3V3 rail instead of the switched display rail the spec describes.\"}",
